  "id": "violation-of-expectation-method",
  "term": "violation-of-expectation method",
  "definition": "The violation-of-expectation method is a research approach that tests understanding by comparing how long infants or toddlers look at an expected event versus one that breaks an expected relationship or rule. Longer looking at the unexpected event is taken as a sign that the child noticed the violation.",
